{"title":"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square is inscribed in a circle of diameter 12. Two vertices of a triangle are also vertices of one side of the square. The other vertex of the triangle is on the circle. Find the largest possible area of the triangle.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the \"base\" of the triangle, which is a side of the square, be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and let the third point of the triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Clearly we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to be as far as possible from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, so we have that the base of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/1/b81097ac54e434963766001e47caa1dcd88003fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> and the height, after some side chasing, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4d10cd187e2a8024df8d423ad1909cbc5b2346d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{12-6\\sqrt{2}}{2}+6\\sqrt{2}=6+3\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"222\" height=\"41\" />. We multiply and divide by 2 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/9/fd9c524dec3928e755e202c0a518131670130e40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{18+18\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"94\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST\">2005 Alabama ARML TST</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspa